⚠️ Bonus Improvement (Parallel Execution)

Your code waits one by one.

Faster version:
var addTwoPromises = async function(p1, p2) {
    const [v1, v2] = await Promise.all([p1, p2]);
    return v1 + v2;
};


👉 Executes both promises in parallel.

✅ Summary (Remember This)

async → returns Promise

await → unwraps Promise

Cleaner async logic

Foundation for APIs, backend, frontend
